---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config.js';

const description =
  'Why AEO Decoded took a break during Season 3, ran deep tests on how AI answer engines cite websites, and came back to basics: people first, principles or tested results — nothing else ships.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Season 3: back to basics, and deeper',
  description,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.author },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.studioName, url: SITE.studioUrl },
  mainEntityOfPage: new URL('/the-reset/', SITE.url).href,
};
---

<Base title="Season 3: Back to Basics" description={description} schema={schema} currentPath="/the-reset/">
  <article class="prose">
    <header class="episode-head">
      <p class="field field--blue">Season 3</p>
      <h1>Season 3: back to basics, and deeper</h1>
      <p class="citable">
        <mark>Season 3 of AEO Decoded comes back to basics: build for people first,
        and every episode is either a principle or a tested result.</mark>
      </p>
    </header>

    <h2>What happened</h2>
    <p>
      Two episodes into recording Season 3, I took a break. The episodes were about
      building AEO into a new site — and the advice in them was true. I'd seen it
      work. But I kept hitting the same honest problem: <em>it all depends on how
      you're set up.</em> Advice that's conditional on your architecture isn't a
      method. It's a maybe.
    </p>
    <p>
      Seasons 1 and 2 covered the fundamentals of Answer Engine Optimization in
      depth, and I stand behind them. But the field around us was filling up with
      tactics — the kind that expire the way SEO tricks always have. I didn't want
      to add to that pile. I didn't want to publish anything I couldn't get behind
      as a genuinely improved approach.
    </p>

    <h2>What the break was for</h2>
    <p>
      How AI answer engines check and cite websites is changing fast. So I used the
      break to run deep tests of my own, and I'll share what I can from those tests
      as Season 3 goes on.
    </p>
    <p>
      The clearest finding so far: a lot of the AI advice and announcements going
      around aren't delivering. So Season 3 goes back to basics and builds back up
      from there. Deal with people first — clear answers, honest expertise, pages
      that actually help the person reading them — and most of the AI details take
      care of themselves.
    </p>

    <h2>What changed</h2>
    <p>
      I also built. The AEO Decoded site — the one you're reading — was moved off
      WordPress and deployed as a custom static architecture on a global edge
      network. No plugins, no database, no bloat between the content and the
      machines reading it. The same standard I built for
      <a href={SITE.studioUrl} rel="noopener">Irishguy Design Studio</a>: perfect
      Lighthouse scores, machine-readable structure, and every AEO principle from
      the show running live on every page.
    </p>
    <p>
      That's the difference between talking about the method and being the method.
      The AEO Decoded site is now the test bench for everything the podcast claims.
    </p>

    <h2>The new standard</h2>
    <p>
      Season 3 runs on one editorial rule: every episode is either a
      <strong>principle</strong> — something true about how machines read the web
      that doesn't expire with the next model release — or a
      <strong>tested result</strong> — something we tried on a real site, measured,
      and can show you. Circulating tactics we can't verify don't ship. If the
      industry is pushing something we haven't proven, we'll test it first and
      report what actually happened.
    </p>

    <h2>What's coming</h2>
    <p>
      Season 3 is a build log, and it goes deeper on each topic. The
      WordPress-to-edge migration you're standing on. The schema layer. The
      measurement system. Results from the tests. And the part nobody in this field
      shows you: tracking whether any of it actually earns citations from ChatGPT,
      Perplexity, and Gemini — in public, with receipts.
    </p>
    <p>
      Seasons 1 and 2 are all here in the
      <a href="/episodes/">AEO Decoded episode archive</a> if you want the
      fundamentals first. Season 3 is where we prove them.
    </p>
    <p>— {SITE.author}</p>

    <section class="cta-strip">
      <p class="field">Follow along</p>
      <h2>Season 3 is live.</h2>
      <p>
        Follow AEO Decoded on your favorite platform to get each new Season 3
        episode the day it publishes.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="/#listen">Choose your podcast platform</a>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
